                <pb facs="1013" n="897" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg897"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.2311/68.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Governor of Texas to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Austin, Tex.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 28, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram asking the consent of the Governor of Texas for a brigade of
                    Mexican Federal troops to enter Texas from Piedras Negras, Coahuila, and proceed
                    to Del Rio and Marathon is received. Under the escort and regulations mentioned
                    by you I have no objection, but we will send rangers to escort them also.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">O. B. Colquitt.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
